From: =?UTF-8?q?Jan=20Drl=C3=BD?= <jd@jandrly.cz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:17:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] sm3: Support several semantics in one I/O register

SM3 allows declaring one register several times with disjoint write masks
(dcl_texcoord0 v0.xy + dcl_texcoord1 v0.zw), and the converter asserted
in dclIoVar on the second declaration. Each semantic now gets its own
variable with the declaration's component mask, and loads and stores
(including the relative addressing switch functions) pick the variable
per component. A component no mask covers belongs to the nearest
declaration below it, else above it.

A semantic declared again (on another mask of the same register, or on
another register), a special register declared twice and an undeclared
register whose implicit semantic is already declared map to the variable
declared first instead of asserting.

Registers with a single declaration are converted exactly as before.
